      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 4.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "sorry I'm a little late, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.02,
      "end_seconds": 9.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.9,
      "end_seconds": 21.99,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "Yeah, mainly light brown spotting. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.96,
      "end_seconds": 27.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.57,
      "end_seconds": 53.44,
      "duration_seconds": 24.87,
      "text": "oh, it's been one week, I'm fairly sure. Oh, and a late period. Had that since last night. And there's a vague low ache as well, one week now. With vague low ache, a three out of ten, I suppose. I'd been feeling slightly dizzy, but that went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.26,
      "end_seconds": 60.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Have you had light brown spotting before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.44,
      "end_seconds": 70.74,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "Actually, you know, a bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.72,
      "end_seconds": 74.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "how about collapse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.63,
      "end_seconds": 79.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "yeah, not at all, no collapse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.15,
      "end_seconds": 83.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Any severe pain, heavy bleeding or shoulder tip pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.53,
      "end_seconds": 88.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "No, um, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.13,
      "end_seconds": 91.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.29,
      "end_seconds": 95.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.69,
      "end_seconds": 113.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.59,
      "end_seconds": 127.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.61,
      "text": "Heart disease, for five years right, I have arthritis in my knees, for nearly five years i've, I've had diabetes for nearly five years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.42,
      "end_seconds": 144.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.55,
      "end_seconds": 149.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.1,
      "end_seconds": 152.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "So, who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.51,
      "end_seconds": 156.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.78,
      "end_seconds": 159.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.86,
      "end_seconds": 166.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "ah, it's aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.31,
      "end_seconds": 167.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "hm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.27,
      "end_seconds": 175.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Right, it's paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed. It's, It's glibenclamide, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.51,
      "end_seconds": 178.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.91,
      "end_seconds": 181.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "5 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.2,
      "end_seconds": 185.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Alright, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.37,
      "end_seconds": 195.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "so, no, not that I know of"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.04,
      "end_seconds": 199.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.51,
      "end_seconds": 212.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Right, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.39,
      "end_seconds": 233.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temp 36.5 degrees. And And pressure 113 over 73, heart rate 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.92,
      "end_seconds": 239.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.13,
      "end_seconds": 243.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.21,
      "end_seconds": 262.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild tenderness low on the left and the pregnancy test is positive."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.15,
      "end_seconds": 275.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "please sit back down having listened and examined, the most likely explanation is a pregnancy of unknown location, ectopic not excluded a threatened miscarriage is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.97,
      "end_seconds": 279.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.62,
      "end_seconds": 297.15,
      "duration_seconds": 14.53,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a pregnancy of unknown location, ectopic not excluded, and we'll know more once the a hormone blood test is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.33,
      "end_seconds": 332.73,
      "duration_seconds": 18.4,
      "text": "I think a hormone blood test makes sense here, for pregnancy of unknown location. I want a pregnancy test done, that's for late period and spotting. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.23,
      "end_seconds": 336.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Well, do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.09,
      "end_seconds": 361.3,
      "duration_seconds": 22.21,
      "text": "Even with little pain this needs a scan within a day, and go to hospital if the pain gets worse. Let's get you seen by the early pregnancy unit, I'll arrange the letter. One warning sign to remember: you get severe pain or feel faint. In that case don't wait. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.36,
      "end_seconds": 365.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "alright, thanks, take care"
    }
  ]
}